meta {
  name: Clone Radiology Panels
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/{{masterDataId}}/radiology-panels/clone
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "targetMasterDataId": "{{targetMasterDataId}}"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  masterDataId: 2db13b5e-4a25-412f-bcd9-68bcbeea9d59
  targetMasterDataId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:master_data__duplicate_test` — enforced by
  `PermissionGuard`; admins bypass, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` succeeds.

  Clone **all active** radiology panels from this master data (the `:masterDataId`
  in the URL, the *source*) into a target master data. Each panel is copied with a
  fresh id and the target's `branchId`, and its member-test rows are remapped onto
  the target's matching radiology tests. Returns `{ "copied": <n>, "skipped": <n> }`.

  A source panel is **skipped** if its `panelName` or `panelCode` already exists
  (active) in the target. Both master data must belong to the caller's tenant (404
  `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND` otherwise).

  Set `targetMasterDataId` to a second (usually different-branch) master data's id.
  The placeholder default will 404 until you set a real id.
}
